WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.021 --> 00:00:02.920
- Social media is filled with
posts that will make you smile

00:00:02.920 --> 00:00:05.270
just a little more. And I like
to share the best of them.

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:06.470
This is What I'm Liking.

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:12.290
All right, so this is one of
my favorite What I'm Liking's.

00:00:12.290 --> 00:00:14.950
The mystic aquarium in
Connecticut goes to great

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:17.500
efforts to make sure the
creatures in their care live their

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:20.400
best lives, y'all. The
animals and fish get toys.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:21.300
It's adorable.

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:24.430
Trainers engage them
in games and exercises,

00:00:24.430 --> 00:00:26.230
but here's the coolest part.

00:00:26.230 --> 00:00:29.840
The aquarium actually brings
in performers to entertain the

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:32.651
sea life. Is that some inception or what?

00:00:32.651 --> 00:00:35.340
They're usually entertaining
us, well you get it? Okay.

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:38.620
Just check out hip hop
violinist Big Lux amusing

00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:41.091
some beluga whales with a little jig.

00:00:41.091 --> 00:00:44.258
(upbeat violin music)

00:00:52.839 --> 00:00:55.089
(applause)

00:00:56.051 --> 00:00:58.160
- If you aren't moved by a beluga whale

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:00.390
watching a violinist play
then you're dead in your

00:01:00.390 --> 00:01:02.810
heart. That is the sweetest thing ever.

00:01:02.810 --> 00:01:06.288
We have Big Lux on the
line watching on NBC 10,

00:01:06.288 --> 00:01:08.480
WJAR Providence.

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:09.333
What's up, man.

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:12.940
- Hey, what's good?

00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:14.170
- Oh my God, well, first of all,

00:01:14.170 --> 00:01:15.930
you have like the greatest smile ever.

00:01:15.930 --> 00:01:18.730
I'm going to lead with that
and beard game, just saying.

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:22.710
It's nice, it's nice. So this is so rad.

00:01:22.710 --> 00:01:24.240
I've never really heard of this,

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:25.370
them hiring entertainment to

00:01:25.370 --> 00:01:27.360
entertain the things that
usually entertain us.

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:29.140
So what's it like playing for whales?

00:01:29.140 --> 00:01:31.400
And it seemed like they liked you.

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:33.290
- It's a crazy, it's
such a crazy experience.

00:01:33.290 --> 00:01:34.680
I mean, you know, who,

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:38.220
whoever gets that opportunity
and you know, they just,

00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:40.600
they just decided to clear
out a little bit of space,

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:43.150
you know, during the day for
me to come in and they said,

00:01:43.150 --> 00:01:44.850
Hey, play whatever you want.

00:01:44.850 --> 00:01:46.760
So I tried to do a whole
bunch of different styles.

00:01:46.760 --> 00:01:48.290
I played hip hop, I played rock.

00:01:48.290 --> 00:01:50.380
I played country music.

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:52.150
And then I play the Irish thing.

00:01:52.150 --> 00:01:53.810
And it was, it was just crazy

00:01:53.810 --> 00:01:56.320
because they would react to
everything so differently.

00:01:56.320 --> 00:01:58.180
They ran away when I played
Devil Went Down to Georgia,

00:01:58.180 --> 00:02:01.367
not feeling it, but I
played that Irish jig

00:02:02.536 --> 00:02:05.210
I played the Irish jig and they
just like jumped right off.

00:02:05.210 --> 00:02:07.110
- Oh my God, well,
they're Irish, it's fine.

00:02:07.110 --> 00:02:09.510
So I love that you play
all different genres.

00:02:09.510 --> 00:02:11.864
We got to get you on the show
to play with us when we do

00:02:11.864 --> 00:02:13.440
one of our like Kelly-oke things.

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:14.473
That'd be so fun.

00:02:15.795 --> 00:02:17.420
So you say this is all part of

00:02:17.420 --> 00:02:19.400
a deeper purpose for you, right?

00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:22.200
- True. I mean, like, I feel
like I'm on my second lifetime.

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:25.470
I was an active duty army for 13 years.

00:02:25.470 --> 00:02:27.140
I was deployed to Baghdad in 2000.

00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:30.487
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh thank
you so much for your service.

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:33.540
- Yeah. I mean, I just feel like

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:34.410
I'm really lucky to be here.

00:02:34.410 --> 00:02:38.040
I was in a, I was in a
bomb searching platoon.

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:40.790
We were combat engineers.
So we got into a lot of,

00:02:40.790 --> 00:02:42.100
a lot of difficult situations.

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:44.060
I didn't think I was
gonna necessarily make it

00:02:44.060 --> 00:02:46.144
back from that experience.

00:02:46.144 --> 00:02:48.240
So I feel like every day is a blessing.

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:50.730
And so I want to use that to
send good vibes to people.

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:53.430
Animals bring people together,
bring animals together.

00:02:56.984 --> 00:02:59.473
- All right, good luck
man, I'm such a fan of you.

00:02:59.473 --> 00:03:01.170
Big Lux, everybody.

00:03:01.170 --> 00:03:03.363
I'm liking your posts right now.

00:03:04.910 --> 00:03:06.410
That's not all though, Big Lux.

00:03:06.410 --> 00:03:08.120
Our season long partner Pilot Pen,

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:10.480
the go-to pen of the Kelly
Clarkson show likes to celebrate

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:13.290
those who create fearlessly
just like you, sir.

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:15.960
So they're going to be using
their friction erasable pen to

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:19.166
write you a check for a thousand
dollars. How's that sound?

00:03:19.166 --> 00:03:21.833
- A thousand dollars? Thank you.

00:03:22.982 --> 00:03:24.532
- [Kelly] I love it. I love it.

00:03:26.006 --> 00:03:26.839
Thank you so much, man.

00:03:26.839 --> 00:03:28.130
I hope you come play with us soon.

